    "title": "Bottom View of a Binary Tree",
    "category": "Trees",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given the root of a binary tree, determine the set of nodes visible when the tree is viewed from the bottom. For every vertical column, only the lowest visible node should be included.",
    "input": "\u2022 The first line contains an integer N. \u2022 The next N lines describe the binary tree.",
    "output": "\u2022 Print the bottom view from leftmost column to rightmost column.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 0 \u2264 N \u2264 2 \u00d7 10^5________________________________________"
